 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, use the graphs and multigraphs in Figure 12.354. In each exercise a graph and a sequence of vertices are given.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 321678,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine whether the sequence of edges, <i>A</i> → <i>B</i> → <i>C</i> → <i>H</i> → <i>G</i> → <i>D</i> → <i>F</i> → <i>E</i>, is an Euler trail, an Euler circuit, or neither for the graph. If it is neither, explain why.",
